{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513366090,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEzOTAxOTI1MjU="},"added":["feedback-desired"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513366090,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEzOTAxOTI1Mjg="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1516141204,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1ODEyNzE2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2032#issuecomment-358127163"},"message":"Just in attempt to answer the formulated question and echoing my whining in #2079, I think that \"by default\" we should:\n- parse all, aggregate, and make available all metadata from the datasets we provide\n- make this metadata easily usable by users\n\nSo what `search` should do differently by default? only that it should be **usable** by users on datasets.datalad.org .  Either it requires any changes to search -- might be not and just educating me how to accomplish the mission!\n\nFor what I meant with \"usable\" -- above  examples are great and worked for me wonderfully, thanks! But  on a larger datasets.datalad.org though, creation of index does take way too long during initial `search` if we index **all** metadata by \"default\".  So \"someone\" should decide to index e.g. only datasets level metadata in such case.  What I was trying to suggest in #2079 is that \"by default\" we might want to search \"dataset\" level metadata only.   But as @mih 's example above nicely demonstrates it is quite feasible in smaller use-cases to index and search through all of metadata, which is sweet.  So, I guess, that is where I, as a curator of the super-dataset, (probably already, as @mih tried to tell me) could state (via config/command `???`) that if someone installs this particular super-dataset (e.g. `///` or even `///openfmri`) -- by default, it should index only dataset-level metadata (even though subdatasets might carry content metadata, and if I install them -- content metadata will be indexed while searching in them)  and let user know about that and include instructions on how to make it index and search across all levels, e.g. with a message: \n```\nINFO: only dataset-level metadata is indexed and searched for this dataset by default.\nINFO: Run XXX to enable indexing also per-file metadata. Note that this operation might take considerable amount of time (minutes or hours) on this large dataset\n```\nSo, may be, such commands/settings as `???` and `XXX` already exist and allow to achieve desired default \"scale-dependent\" behavior?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1516185187,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1ODI2MzYyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2032#issuecomment-358263627"},"message":"\u003e For what I meant with \"usable\" -- above examples are great and worked for me wonderfully, thanks! \n\nGreat. That's what I wasn't sure about in previous discussions and that's what I first and foremost wanted to know by means of the hangout I proposed in #2079 .","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518255911,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NDYzOTUzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2032#issuecomment-364639537"},"message":"With #2127 `search` does all that. At least in principle. Once we have new-style aggregated metadata for `///` we can test and fix any remaining issues that come up.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1526114411,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTYyMzExODQ3Mw=="},"status":2}]}